    {
      "title": "Russian society being ‘systematically crushed’ says Novaya Gazeta as newspaper announces closure",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/30/novaya-gazeta-russia-independent-newspaper-to-close",
      "description": "<p>Independent outlet, whose former editor Dmitry Muratov won Nobel prize, cites intolerable pressure from authorities</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/30/spain-investigates-toledo-crash-pedro-sanchez-france-italy-protests-latest-news-updates\">Europe live – latest updates</a></p></li></ul><p>Novaya Gazeta, one of Russia’s best-known independent media outlets, has announced it will permanently close next month. The newspaper, whose former editor-in-chief Dmitry Muratov <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/oct/08/my-nobel-peace-prize-belongs-to-russias-murdered-journalists-says-dmitry-muratov\">won the Nobel peace prize in 2021</a>, cited intolerable pressure, including being stripped of its newsroom, its donation platforms and its legal right to publish.</p><p>“This is not just our own story; it is the story of a country and a society that are being systematically crushed,” wrote its editor-in-chief, Sergei Sokolov, on the newspaper’s website.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/30/novaya-gazeta-russia-independent-newspaper-to-close\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-30T15:52:51"
    },
    {
      "title": "People of 27 nationalities may be among those killed or injured in Spain train crash, Sánchez says – as it happened",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/30/spain-investigates-toledo-crash-pedro-sanchez-france-italy-protests-latest-news-updates",
      "description": "<p>This blog is now closed, you can read more on this story <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/30/spain-trust-high-speed-rail-broken-after-second-deadly-crash-this-year-says-pedro-sanchez\">here</a></p><p><strong>Peunte</strong> begins by paying tribute to all affected by the incident.</p><p>He says that <strong>“at present, evidence points to a failure within Adif’s command and control centre,”</strong> but adds that investigators are still looking “to clarify what exactly happened.” He says he still has confidence in the system.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/30/spain-investigates-toledo-crash-pedro-sanchez-france-italy-protests-latest-news-updates\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
