    {
      "title": "Cost of living protests  to spread to Germany and reignite in France on Halloween",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/30/cost-of-living-protests-to-spread-to-germany-and-reignite-in-france-on-halloween",
      "description": "<p>Activists call for people to make their anger known over poor public services including education and housing</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/30/spain-investigates-toledo-crash-pedro-sanchez-france-italy-protests-latest-news-updates\">Europe live – latest updates</a></p></li></ul><p>Street protests sweeping Europe are expected to spread to Germany and reignite in France on Saturday, with police mobilised to stop potential looting and rioting on the fringes of what organisers hope will be peaceful rallies.</p><p>Weeks of, <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/18/europe-protests-france-spain-portugal-2026-explainer\">at times violent, student demonstrations</a> have rocked Italy, Spain, Portugal, Albania and France, where activists on Halloween have again called for people to make their anger over the cost of living and deficient public services felt across the country.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/30/cost-of-living-protests-to-spread-to-germany-and-reignite-in-france-on-halloween\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-30T14:42:46"
    },
    {
      "title": "Friday briefing: Israel has a dilemma - can its opposition govern with Palestinian parties?",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/30/friday-briefing-israel-has-a-dilemma-can-its-opposition-govern-with-palestinian-parties",
      "description": "<p>In today’s newsletter: Benjamin Netanyahu has been left without a majority, now it is up to the coalition to find out whether the desire for change will prove to be a defining political moment</p><p>Good morning. It was described by many Israelis as the most consequential election in their country’s history. And, as the final votes were tallied, it has delivered a result that presents Israel with a significant dilemma.</p><p>Benjamin Netanyahu’s far-right coalition has lost its mandate while the opposition has a clear majority: but only if the Jewish Israeli opposition bloc, led by retired general Gadi Eisenkot, is prepared to make a governing pact with Palestinian Israeli parties, which have secured a historic result.</p><p><em><strong>UK politics </strong></em>| John Healey <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/oct/29/john-healey-budget-backs-away-from-cutting-welfare-public-finance-shortfall\">has backed away</a> from cutting the cost of welfare this parliament, amid dire warnings his first budget could lead to brutal spending cuts because of a £28bn shortfall in public finances.</p><p><em><strong>Patrick Stewart </strong></em>| The acclaimed British stage and screen actor renowned for both Shakespeare and sci-fi,<a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2026/oct/29/patrick-stewart-dead\"> died at his home </a>in Los Angeles after “a brief and poignant journey with Alzheimer’s disease and Lewy body dementia”, his longtime spokesperson said.</p><p><em><strong>Environment </strong></em>| One of the most <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/oct/30/wildlife-trusts-northumberland-nature-recovery-rothbury-estate\">ambitious nature recovery projects</a> ever undertaken in England can go ahead after campaigners announced they had raised £30m to buy an estate in Northumberland.</p><p><em><strong>Europe </strong></em>| Spain began three days of mourning on Thursday for at least 69 people <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/29/spain-mourning-period-deadly-train-crash\">who died in a high-speed rail collision</a>, as hospitals continued to treat dozens of injured passengers and train drivers went on strike to urge more investment in railway safety.</p><p><em><strong>US news </strong></em>| The Trump administration <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/29/trump-administration-california-noncitizen-voting-investigation\">has opened a criminal investigation </a>in California over claims that thousands of noncitizens are registered to vote in the state, and has begun subpoenaing election officials.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/30/friday-briefing-israel-has-a-dilemma-can-its-opposition-govern-with-palestinian-parties\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-30T06:44:29"
    },
